      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $- 3 x^{2}\\tan x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=- 3 x^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(- 3 x^{2})'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 3 x^{2})\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(- 6 x)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 3 x^{2})(\\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=- 6 x \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(- 3 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
